ta","html_url":"https://github.com/acamarata","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acamarata/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acamarata/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acamarata/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acamarata/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acamarata/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acamarata/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acamarata/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acamarata/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acamarata/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"jobs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/acamarata/cascade/actions/runs/34616832466/jobs","logs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/acamarata/cascade/actions/runs/34616832466/logs","check_suite_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/acamarata/cascade/check-suites/93775164868","artifacts_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/acamarata/cascade/actions/runs/34616832466/artifacts","cancel_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/acamarata/cascade/actions/runs/34616832466/cancel","rerun_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/acamarata/cascade/actions/runs/34616832466/rerun","previous_attempt_url":null,"workflow_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/acamarata/cascade/actions/workflows/349600391","head_commit":{"id":"6e95bc0d75276073284717ad6fde24f1460e0ccc","tree_id":"4673a5697223f5a42eedfa259cf4bf32bad30e84","message":"feat(core): land PEWS lifecycle, fleet headroom, FLOW primitives; fix a gate that scanned its own fixture\n\nTickets: the PEWS ticket lifecycle, the dogfood conversion of this phase's own\nplan, the fleet headroom model with backpressure, and the conductor FLOW\nprimitives.\n\nThe dogfood conversion is the one that earned its keep. Run against the real\n405-ticket plan it found that seven files carry fields outside the closed\nschema, and the engine refused the entire load rather than silently dropping\nthem, which is the correct behavior and the opposite of what this phase keeps\nfinding elsewhere. That acceptance criterion is reported NOT MET rather than\nworked around; the plan tree and the schema are both outside that ticket's\nscope to change.\n\nFixes a gate that failed on its own evidence. The SPORT registry's real-tree\nscan was reading internal/build/testdata/seeded-violations, where a fixture\ncarries a deliberately malformed SPORT marker so the gate can be proven to\nturn red. Scanning it as ordinary source made the registry ungenerable. It was\ninvisible locally for a sharp reason worth recording: the scan reads git\nls-files, and the fixture was still untracked while the gate was written and\nverified, so it went green every local run and red the first time CI saw it.\nA gate verified against a working tree is not verified against the tree CI sees.\n\nThree tickets are filed BLOCKED rather than shipped. Cost attribution is\nmoney-critical and needed a cross-package migration pattern the agent could not\nverify in budget. The routing-matrix goldens turned up a real contradiction:\n\"cost-tie\" is not a producible outcome, because an earlier filter collapses the\ncandidate set to one before the cost filter runs, which the file's own header\nalready admits. The lane bench protocol landed its core and stopped short of\nthe parts needing live credentials and a running daemon.","timestamp":"2026-09-11T15:33:27Z","author":{"name":"Aric Camarata","email":"aric.camarata@gmail.com"},"committer":{"name":"Aric Camarata","email":"aric.camarata@gmail.com"}},"repository":{"id":1352289740,"node_id":"R_kgDOUJpNzA","name":"cascade","full_name":"acamarata/cascade","private":false,"owner":{"login":"acamarata","id":277910,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NzkxMA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/277910?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/acamarata","html_url":"https://github.c